    "judgment": {
      "status": "confirmed",
      "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. q-9302: the disk has radius 2, so its area is 4\\pi; |det(T)|=10 gives image area 40\\pi. q-8516: (8\\cos150°,8\\sin150°)=(-4\\sqrt{3},4). q-120455: r^2=(-3)^2+(\\sqrt{3})^2=12, so B=(12\\cos(11\\pi/6),12\\sin(11\\pi/6))=(6\\sqrt{3},-6). q-102975: the logarithm requires x>-5/3, and monotonicity gives x\\le(e^2-5)/3. q-102979: the logarithms require 1/4<x<4; comparing their arguments gives x\\ge8/17. q-21063: the vertices map to (6,3), (8,4), and (10,5), producing the entire segment from (6,3) to (10,5). Current option 1 depicts that same segment; the source image additionally marks its interior point (8,4). q-21058: the vertices map to (2,10), (3,15), and (5,25), producing the entire segment from (2,10) to (5,25). Current option 1 depicts that same segment; the source image additionally marks (3,15). These image-display differences are mathematically equivalent. q-162206: det(T)=-1, so the invertible transformation preserves a nondegenerate quadrilateral. q-162199: the zero matrix maps every point to the origin. q-88495: the four simple roots -2,0,2,6 give alternating signs, positive on (-\\infty,-2), (0,2), and (6,\\infty), with roots excluded. q-42259: BC=(7,1)^T and A(BC)=(7,15,9)^T. q-41981: AB=(2,11) and (AB)C=(-3,5). q-42264: only statement II is always true, by associativity; the other statements require commutativity. q-130455: only statement I is always true; distribution gives AB-AC, and AC=CA is not guaranteed. q-78497: multiplying F by itself gives rows (3,12) and (4,19). q-130510: rearranging gives 3x-4y=1 and 0x+y=-4, yielding the selected matrix equation. No submitted grades are supplied; confirmation rests on the captured worked solutions and independent calculations.",
